{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs6ym17u4Ci1VUmWzMPJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The bug was mutable default arguments in `inv/warehouse.py`. The test now passes (1 passed), and it's the only test in the repo. I haven't committed anything.\n\n- **Shared state:** `Warehouse.__init__(self, name, stock={}, history=[])` created one dict and one list when the function was defined. Every warehouse built without those arguments shared them, so a second warehouse showed the first one's stock and `restock` on one changed the other.\n- **Second instance of the same bug:** `restock(..., tags=[])` passed that default list straight into each new `Item`, so every item restocked without tags shared one tag list.\n\nThe fix uses `None` defaults and builds the dict and lists inside the function. `restock` now copies any `tags` you pass in, so an item no longer shares a list with the caller. The signatures are otherwise unchanged, so callers that pass `stock` or `history` explicitly work as before.\n\nI didn't change the test."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1511,"cache_read_input_tokens":39830,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1511},"output_tokens":308,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bbb7e876-13be-41ba-9089-158da80a0568","uuid":"94ee524a-c356-44cb-b078-78d822366621","timestamp":"2026-10-09T18:03:34.954Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs6yki1DETdAeD26z761"}
